// Exercises a per-case custom event schema (event.dwschema): the event
// kinds are author-defined (`attempt` is the decision kind, `outcome` is
// history — NOT request/response), and the injected principal field is
// renamed `actor` (not `callerPrincipal`).
//
// A Read is permitted only if the SAME actor formerly logged in. The
// correlation compares the past Login's `actor` field to `principal`
// — which resolves to the request's scope principal, independent of what
// the schema names its injected principal field. (The event schema's role
// is to *declare* `actor` so the predicate validates; the value comes from
// the trace, and the request principal comes from the trace's scope.)
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::attempt{ input.user: context.input.user, actor: principal }
};
